> who was Pericles
**assistant**:
> Pericles was a prominent and influential statesman, orator, and general of Athens during its Golden Age, specifically the time between the Persian and Peloponnesian wars. He lived from 495 to 429 BCE. Pericles is best known for his leadership in developing Athens into a great cultural and intellectual center and was instrumental in advancing democracy. Under his leadership, the Acropolis and the Parthenon were constructed, and Athens became an empire of sorts. His era, often referred to as the "Age of Pericles," was marked by great artistic and political achievements.
